<BrandLogos />

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════
     WHY SOLYX FOR PHILADELPHIA
══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="sx-why">
  <div class="sx-why__container">

    <div class="sx-why__image-wrap">
      <img
        src="/images/solyx-window-film-philadelphia-why.jpg"
        alt="Comfortable evenly lit Philadelphia law office interior with large windows, warm soft natural light, attorneys relaxed"
        title="Solyx window film for Philadelphia offices — privacy and solar control"
        width="768"
        height="1376"
        loading="lazy"
        class="sx-why__image"
      />
      <div class="sx-why__stat-card">
        <div class="sx-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>700+ designs across Geometric &amp; Organic collections</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sx-why__stat-divider"></div>
        <div class="sx-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>Frosted, gradient, solar, and safety in one brand</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sx-why__content">
      <span class="sx-why__eyebrow">Why Solyx for Philadelphia</span>
      <h2 class="sx-why__headline">Philadelphia's Open-Plan Offices and Historic Glass Are What Solyx Was Designed For.</h2>
      <p class="sx-why__intro">
        Philadelphia's commercial real estate runs on open-plan layouts — open studios, co-working floors, glass-walled conference rooms, and lobby-facing reception desks. That environment demands <a href="/benefits/privacy/" class="sx-body-link">privacy solutions</a> that look intentional, not improvised. Solyx gradient and frosted films address that need directly, without construction and without the permanence of etched or sandblasted glass. "With more than 700 designs, there's a film for every style," according to Decorative Films, LLC (<a href="https://www.decorativefilm.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="sx-body-link">decorativefilm.com</a>), the manufacturer of the SOLYX® window film brand. For properties that also need solar performance — Philadelphia's west-facing <a href="/applications/office/" class="sx-body-link">Center City offices</a> face significant afternoon heat gain — Solyx UltraCool fills that role alongside the decorative lineup.
      </p>
      <ul class="sx-why__bullets">
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Philadelphia rowhome bathrooms and sidelights get frosted privacy without replacing or obscuring historic glass</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Center City conference rooms and office partitions get gradient and patterned films that look architectural, not applied</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Solyx film installer for Philadelphia properties carries UltraCool-IR8360, a Nano Ceramic polyester film with spectrally selective IR blocking, for solar heat management without dark tint</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span><a href="/benefits/uv-protection/" class="sx-body-link">UV protection</a> is built into Solyx functional films — 99%+ UV block on UltraCool and UltraSafe series products</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>UltraSafe Safety Films are available in 2, 4, and 8 mil clear construction — holding broken glass together after impact at Philadelphia retail, schools, and healthcare facilities</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="sx-why__climate-facts">
        <div class="sx-why__climate-item">
          <span class="sx-why__climate-num">700+</span>
          <span class="sx-why__climate-label">Solyx film designs</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sx-why__climate-item">
          <span class="sx-why__climate-num">8 mil</span>
          <span class="sx-why__climate-label">Max UltraSafe thickness</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sx-why__climate-item">
          <span class="sx-why__climate-num">99%+</span>
          <span class="sx-why__climate-label">UV block, functional films</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact/" class="sx-why__cta">
        Get a free film assessment &rarr;
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12h15m0 0l-6.75-6.75M19.5 12l-6.75 6.75"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════
     RESIDENTIAL / COMMERCIAL SLIDER
══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="sx-slider" id="sxSlider">
  <div class="sx-slider__track" id="sxTrack">

    <!-- SLIDE 01: Residential -->
    <div class="sx-slider__slide" data-slide="0">
      <img src="/images/solyx-window-film-philadelphia-residential.jpg" alt="Bright comfortable Philadelphia rowhome living room with Solyx frosted privacy window film on street-facing glass"
          title="Solyx residential window film for Philadelphia rowhomes" class="sx-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="sx-slider__overlay"></div>
      <div class="sx-slider__content">
        <div class="sx-slider__step">01</div>
        <h2 class="sx-slider__title">Philadelphia Rowhomes Run on Solyx Privacy</h2>
        <p class="sx-slider__desc">Street-facing glass, bathroom windows, and sidelights are where Philadelphia homeowners discover Solyx first. Frosted and gradient films solve the privacy problem that replacing glass can't — they let light through while keeping sightlines out, and they look like they belong on the window.</p>
        <div class="sx-slider__faq">
          <div class="sx-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="sx-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Which Solyx film is best for a rowhome bathroom?<span class="sx-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="sx-slider__faq-a" hidden>Solyx Frosted Privacy Films are the most common choice — they provide full visual privacy while allowing natural light to diffuse through. For a more design-forward result, a gradient film fading from frosted at the top to clear at the bottom gives privacy where it matters while preserving a view at eye level. We'll show samples during your free consultation.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="sx-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="sx-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will Solyx film change how my home looks from the street?<span class="sx-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="sx-slider__faq-a" hidden>Frosted Solyx films have a subtle matte appearance from the exterior that reads as etched or sandblasted glass — architectural rather than applied. Clear-background films like UltraCool are nearly invisible. We'll show you exterior samples before any installation so you know exactly what to expect.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="sx-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="sx-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can Solyx film go on historic Philadelphia windows?<span class="sx-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="sx-slider__faq-a" hidden>Yes. Solyx decorative and frosted films are applied to the interior glass surface and do not permanently alter the glass. For historic single-pane glass in older Philadelphia rowhomes, interior application means the film can be removed if needed without affecting the original glass. We assess glass type and condition before every installation.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="sx-slider__cta">Get a residential estimate &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SLIDE 02: Commercial -->
    <div class="sx-slider__slide" data-slide="1">
      <img src="/images/solyx-window-film-philadelphia-commercial.jpg" alt="Modern Center City Philadelphia open-plan office with Solyx gradient window film on conference room glass walls"
          title="Solyx commercial window film for Philadelphia offices" class="sx-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="sx-slider__overlay"></div>
      <div class="sx-slider__content">
        <div class="sx-slider__step">02</div>
