      <p class="sx-pl-row__body">Gradient films fade from frosted to clear — or clear to frosted — across a single glass panel. The effect creates a visual boundary without a physical one: frosted at seated eye level for privacy, clear below for sightlines and connection to the floor, clear above for natural light to pass through. In Philadelphia open-plan offices, this is the most elegant solution to the conference room fishbowl problem — it delivers meaningful privacy without making the space feel closed off.</p>
      <p class="sx-pl-row__body">Available in single-direction fades (frosted top to clear bottom, or clear top to frosted bottom) and dual-direction fades (frosted at both edges, clear in the center), SOLYX® Gradient Films come in standard heights of 60" and 71" for floor-to-ceiling glass applications. For non-standard dimensions or fully custom gradients, the SolyxIQ digital print platform enables precise custom fade patterns at commercial scale — including color gradients, branded content, and multi-panel installations that read as a single continuous image across a glass wall.</p>
