      <h3 class="sx-pl-row__heading">SOLYX® UltraSafe Series — Glass Retention in 2, 4, and 8 Mil Clear Construction</h3>
      <p class="sx-pl-row__body">Glass is the weakest point in most buildings. When it breaks — from a smash-and-grab, an accident, or a weather event — the shards are the hazard. SOLYX® UltraSafe Safety Films are applied to the interior glass surface where, on impact, they hold a broken pane together rather than letting it scatter. The series runs from the 2 mil UltraSafe-260 for light safety glazing requirements up to the 8 mil UltraSafe-860 for high-demand applications in schools, government facilities, and retail storefronts.</p>
      <p class="sx-pl-row__body">In Philadelphia, UltraSafe is most commonly installed on Old City and South Street retail storefronts for smash-and-grab deterrence, K-12 schools and university buildings for safety glazing upgrades, and healthcare facilities with high public foot traffic. The SXGF-0500 Clear Frosted Safety Film combines frosted privacy with the glass retention function of the UltraSafe series — a dual-purpose product for applications that need both benefits. Important: UltraSafe holds glass together on impact. It does not make glass unbreakable.</p>
