<section class="sx-faq" id="faq">
  <div class="sx-faq__inner">
    <div class="sx-faq__header fade-in">
      <span class="sx-eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="sx-faq__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p>Honest answers about Solyx window film in Philadelphia from specialists with over 15 years of installation experience.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="sx-faq__cta-btn">Talk to a Specialist</a>
    </div>
    <div class="sx-faq__list fade-in">
      <div class="sx-faq__item sx-faq__item--open">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>What is Solyx window film?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Solyx is a specialty window film brand by Decorative Films, LLC offering over 700 designs across decorative, privacy, solar control, and safety film categories. Window Film Philadelphia is an authorized Solyx installer serving residential and commercial properties throughout Philadelphia.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>What makes Solyx different from other window film brands in Philadelphia?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Solyx is built around the broadest decorative and specialty film library in the category — over 700 patterns across Geometric and Organic collections, plus functional solar and safety films. Where most brands focus primarily on solar control, Solyx is the right choice when design, privacy, and glass aesthetics matter as much as performance.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>Does Solyx make solar control film or just decorative film?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Solyx makes both. The SOLYX® UltraCool series includes solar control films with IR blocking and UV protection for heat and glare management. The UltraSafe series provides safety and security glass retention films. These functional lines pair with Solyx decorative and frosted products for comprehensive glass treatment solutions in Philadelphia properties.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>What is the difference between Solyx Frosted and Gradient film?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Solyx Frosted Privacy Films provide a consistent opacity across the entire glass surface — like etched or sandblasted glass. Gradient Films transition from frosted to clear across a single panel, typically frosted at seated eye level for privacy and clear above and below to preserve light and sightlines. Gradient is popular for Philadelphia conference rooms and open-plan office partitions.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>Can Solyx film be used in a Philadelphia rowhome bathroom?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Yes. Solyx Frosted Privacy Films are among the most popular applications for Philadelphia rowhome bathrooms, sidelights, and street-facing ground-floor windows. They provide full visual privacy while allowing natural light to pass through — without changing the character of the window from the exterior.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>Are Solyx decorative pattern films permanent?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Solyx decorative films are semi-permanent — they use pressure-sensitive adhesive that holds firmly through normal use but can be removed when needed. This makes them a practical choice for leased Philadelphia commercial spaces where permanent modifications may not be permitted, and for properties where branding or design may evolve over time.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>What is UltraCool-IR8360 and is it right for Philadelphia summers?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>UltraCool-IR8360 is a Nano Ceramic polyester solar control film engineered for spectrally selective IR blocking. It targets infrared heat while allowing visible light through, reducing solar heat gain without a dark or reflective appearance. For Philadelphia's west- and south-facing office and residential glass, it is a practical solar upgrade with a high-clarity result.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>Can Solyx UltraSafe film protect Philadelphia retail against smash-and-grab?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Solyx UltraSafe Safety Films hold broken glass together after impact, which slows forced entry and reduces the risk of injury from flying shards. Available in 2, 4, and 8 mil clear construction, UltraSafe is installed on interior glass surfaces at Philadelphia retail storefronts, schools, and commercial properties where glass retention is a priority. It delays entry — it does not make glass unbreakable.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>Does Solyx work on double-pane or single-pane windows in Philadelphia?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Solyx decorative and frosted films are generally suitable for both single-pane and double-pane glass when applied to the interior surface. For solar control films on insulated glass units, compatibility depends on the specific film and glass construction. Window Film Philadelphia assesses glass type and orientation before recommending a film to ensure compatibility and long-term performance.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sx-faq__item">
        <div class="sx-faq__q"><span>How does Window Film Philadelphia install Solyx decorative film?</span><span class="sx-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="sx-faq__a"><p>Our team performs a site assessment to evaluate glass type, dimensions, and the installation environment. Solyx films are applied wet to the interior glass surface using professional-grade tools, then trimmed to fit and smoothed flat. Decorative and frosted films reach full adhesion within a few days, after which they perform as a durable, cleanable part of the glass surface.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

